// workspace_name_prefix.proto — the marks drawn immediately BEFORE a
// workspace's name, wherever a client draws that name: the sidebar's row
// (frontend.v1.RosterRowName.prefix), the topbar's name line
// (frontend.v1.TopbarWorkspaceName.prefix), and every Emacs surface that
// reads the roster row (the tab bar, the SPC p p / SPC p P switcher).
//
// ONE MESSAGE FOR EVERY SURFACE. The prefix is resolved once in the daemon
// (agent-repld internal/resolve/nameprefix), drawn by one helper per client
// (the webapp's src/name-prefix.ts, the editor's
// `agent-repl-name-prefix-string' in lisp/status.el), and every surface that
// draws a workspace's name draws its prefix through that helper. A new mark is
// one new field here and one new branch in each of those helpers, never a
// second per-surface message.
//
// THE DRAWN ORDER IS THE FIELD ORDER, left to right, and the order is fixed:
//
//   1. the priority icon (priority, field 1);
//   2. the emoji-ack glyph (emoji_ack, field 2), to the right of the priority
//      icon (owner request, 2026-11-19).
//
// The two are independent: a workspace may wear either, both, or neither.
// The emoji-ack glyph first landed as a glyph message of each name element
// (design record docs/protobuf-design/2026-11-18-emoji-ack-name-glyph.md);
// it lives here now, so both marks are decided, ordered and drawn as one.
//
// A name that wears no mark carries NO prefix at all: the field is UNSET,
// never set empty. A set prefix carrying no mark is a malformed view.
//
// A mark is never part of the name's text: the name is a slug every verb
// resolves (rename, workspace prompt NAME, the branch and worktree directory),
// so a mark is a drawn thing beside it.

